(particularly under negation), but weak after prepositions. Separate lexical
responses cover Chinese any, hand, mobile phone, meat, and Android imports.
Hand and meat are also recognized across UTF-8 fragments, with a larger
response after whitespace. The unfinished two-byte prefix of meat is
recognized there too. Fruit pulp receives a weaker response than meat.
Most other tokens contribute approximately zero.
