"""Approximate rare formatting responses, leaving ordinary text near zero.

Positive: backslashes and newline escapes extending escaped whitespace;
most strongly, the colon of a document-initial 'Title:' label. Negative:
nonbreaking-space chunks and following double backticks, TeX text/font
argument braces, and the emoji variation selector. Minor rules cover
initial raw whitespace and repeated middle dots. Chunk sizes matter for
nonbreaking-space formatting, so this is not a general whitespace counter.
All context is a short text tail, reset at document boundaries.
