Positive responses include astronomy stems and a few physical/spatial phrases.
A separate spelling response distinguishes short tr- continuations: a followed
by m/n is negative, whereas o/u followed by m is positive. Transliteration
shares the spelling rules across alphabets. Token boundaries matter.
These rules summarize recurring training responses, not all lexical variation.
The state stores the preceding token and unfinished word, reset per document.
Other tokens get zero, apart from a small document-start offset.
